"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[],"properties":{"securityScore":100,"primaryLanguage":"JSON","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789134492.6724741,"endTime":1789134510.345233}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"brainstorming","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5722sqpkcx1fyy5yaahvcm7458e708a-0hcf5L/clawscan-skillspector-2377585537/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T13:48:10.900800+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":33,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":54,"executable":false,"size_bytes":2505,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"_meta.json","type":"json","lines":6,"executable":false,"size_bytes":132,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-c1c49504a5ac4a88b4b1ef0694a229a0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill description says it 'MUST' be used before any creative work, including very common development activities like creating features, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. That makes the invocation scope excessively broad and likely to trigger in many normal workflows, which can inappropriately route unrelated tasks through this skill and increase the chance of unnecessary repository inspection or follow-on actions. In context, this is more dangerous because the skill also instructs checking project files/commits and later writing documents and committing to git.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger conditions to specific planning or design-request scenarios instead of 'any creative work.' Replace mandatory language like 'MUST use this before any creative work' with explicit, user-driven invocation criteria, such as using the skill only when the user asks for brainstorming, requirements clarification, or design exploration.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9ade13149e71441e94267fbc0625b5e9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":37,"end_line":40},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs the agent to write a design document to docs/plans and commit it to git, but it does not require explicit user confirmation immediately before those state-changing actions. This is risky because creating files and making commits modifies the user's workspace and version history; combined with the skill's broad invocation scope, these actions could occur during routine ideation without the user realizing the skill will persist changes.","remediation":"Add an explicit consent gate before any file creation or git activity. Require the skill to clearly warn the user that it is about to write a document and create a commit, and proceed only after a specific confirmation; alternatively, make documentation and git steps optional suggestions rather than automatic instructions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":37,"end_line":40}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1388,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1402},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1999,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2013},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","us